.TH "GLESHA-STATUS" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-status \- show the state, size, and cost of backup sets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha status\fR [SET] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the condition, snapshot count, stored size, and estimated yearly storage cost of every set, or of SET only.
.PP
Values come from local state. Use \-\-refresh to query the remotes for archive availability; no retrieval is requested. A '\-' marks a value that is unknown, not zero.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Query the remotes for archive availability.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha status
glesha status docs \-\-refresh
glesha status \-\-format csv
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-history (1),
.BR glesha\-list (1)
